{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And from the hand of a foreigner.</b> Who brought an offering by the hand of a priest to offer it to the heavens — <b>you shall not offer</b> to Him one with a blemish. And even though animals with blemishes were not forbidden for the offerings of the children of Noaḥ unless missing a limb — that practice applies to a roadside altar in the fields, but upon the altar in the Tabernacle you shall not offer them; however, you may accept unblemished ones from them. Therefore it is stated above, ״אִישׁ אִישׁ״ — to include the nations, who vow vows and freewill offerings like Israel (Ḥullin 13)." "<b>Corruption.</b> Their marring." "<b>They shall not be acceptable for you.</b> To atone for you."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:48.411659338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}